[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2484219025","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99254#issuecomment-2484219025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99254","id":2484219025,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UEiyR","user":{"login":"dbnicholson","id":6495518,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTU1MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6495518?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbnicholson","html_url":"https://github.com/dbnicholson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbnicholson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbnicholson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbnicholson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbnicholson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbnicholson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbnicholson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbnicholson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbnicholson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbnicholson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-18T21:59:21Z","updated_at":"2024-11-18T21:59:21Z","body":"> However, this is always printed when `--fail-on-error` is used when `SceneTree.quit()` is called (since its default value is 0):\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> WARNING: Cannot set exit code to 0 after an error has occurred.\r\n>      at: set_exit_code (./core/os/os.cpp:221)\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> Code used:\r\n> \r\n> ```gdscript\r\n> func _ready() -> void:\r\n> \tpush_error(\"Error\")\r\n> \tget_tree().quit()\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nShould I drop the warning? It was my minor attempt at highlighting to users why `quit()` may not be doing what they expect, but I'm not sure it's adding any value. I could also change it to a `WARN_VERBOSE` or put it under `DEV_ENABLED` or something.\r\n\r\n> This does not occur if the engine is exited via other methods, e.g. `--quit`.\r\n\r\nIt still exit's unsuccessfully with `--fail-on-error --quit`, though, right?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2484219025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2484247171","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99254#issuecomment-2484247171","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99254","id":2484247171,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UEpqD","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-18T22:15:52Z","updated_at":"2024-11-18T22:16:07Z","body":"> Should I drop the warning? \r\n\r\nYes, I'd move it to `WARN_VERBOSE()`.\r\n\r\n> It still exit's unsuccessfully with --fail-on-error --quit, though, right?\r\n\r\nYes, exit code is still `1` as evidenced by calling `echo $?` after